      "ocr_text": "RJR\nSEORET\nINTEROFFICE MMDRANDUMN0.3 5 5_By\nMarch 30, 1987\nMr. K. L. Rush\nTO:\nFROM: R. L. McGee\nsuBJect: Qualification of Alcoa Substrate\nThis is to reiterate our comments madc in the Transition Meeting\nof Tuesday, March 24, 1987, regarding the qualification of Alcoa\nas a supplier of substrate. t is critical that we make every\neffort to identify the acceptability of Alcoa's product by June\n1, i987, in order to allow us to effectively negotiate with w. R.\nGrace regarding their material.\nYou are probably well aware that we'are currently paying\nolb. or race matrial versus a prie of sb.which\nwould be charged for Alcoa material. additionally Grace would\nincur capital expenditures amounting to greater than $55,ooo,000\nto expand facilities to meet our requirements, and has suggested\nthat we provide the capital for the expansion project. Alcoa has\nadvised that they would incur all costs for any cxpansion and\nwould maintain their price at current level or lower.\nGrace has advised that they need to bc given a dcfinite answer on\nour\nintentions by July 1, 19e7, in order to initiate the\nexpansion program which they have proposed to us. Alcoa's\nqualification will enable us to negotiate with them from a\nposition of strength.\nhesitate to contact us should you wish to discuss this issue\nwe\napprcciate your efforts in this matter. Please do not\nfurther.\nThank you.\nFekut\nRobert L. McGee\nRLM/ms\n2199 st9os\nMr. R. J. Reagan\ncC:\nMr. R. G. Haberkern",
